#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1391
msgid "Sets the number of copies to generate from the original layer."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1395
msgid ""
"Delays each copy’s animation by a set number of milliseconds. This delay is "
"added on top of the previous one, so it accumulates for each additional "
"copy. One second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1399
#, no-php-format
msgid ""
"Shifts each copy’s position horizontally by the specified amount, as if they "
"were created at an offset location from the original. The shift is "
"cumulative when using fixed values, so each copy is placed further from the "
"previous one. When using randomized values or expressions, however, each "
"copy is calculated independently and the shift is not cumulative. You can "
"use positive and negative values. Randomized values are also supported, but "
"avoid mixing units. Supported units: <ul><li><b>px:</b> A fixed value "
"specified in pixels.<br><br></li><li><b>sw:</b> Percentage of the slider "
"width. 1sw equals to 1% of the slider width. This value scales dynamically "
"when the slider’s size changes.<br><br></li><li><b>lw:</b> Percentage of the "
"layer width. 1lw equals to 1% of the layer width. This value scales "
"dynamically when the layer’s size changes.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1403
#, no-php-format
msgid ""
"Shifts each copy’s position vertically by the specified amount, as if they "
"were created at an offset location from the original. The shift is "
"cumulative when using fixed values, so each copy is placed further from the "
"previous one. When using randomized values or expressions, however, each "
"copy is calculated independently and the shift is not cumulative. You can "
"use positive and negative values. Randomized values are also supported, but "
"avoid mixing units. Supported units: <ul><li><b>px:</b> A fixed value "
"specified in pixels.<br><br></li><li><b>sh:</b> Percentage of the slider "
"height. 1sh equals to 1% of the slider height. This value scales dynamically "
"when the slider’s size changes.<br><br></li><li><b>lh:</b> Percentage of the "
"layer height. 1lh equals to 1% of the layer height. This value scales "
"dynamically when the layer’s size changes.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1407
msgid ""
"Defines the lower limit of the opacity applied across copies. By default, "
"copies gradually fade between the Max and Min values, and the distribution "
"is controlled by the Fade Method setting."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1411
msgid ""
"Defines the upper limit of the opacity applied across copies. By default, "
"copies gradually fade between the Max and Min values, and the distribution "
"is controlled by the Fade Method setting."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1415
msgid ""
"Determines how opacity values are distributed between the Max and Min "
"settings across copies. Different methods use various curves to define the "
"progression, creating either even or non-linear value sequences."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1419
msgid ""
"Adjusts the scale transformation for each additional copy by the specified "
"step value. Positive values progressively enlarge copies, while negative "
"values shrink them. When using random values, each copy will receive a "
"randomly chosen value from the defined range. When using cycle values, "
"copies will take the defined values in order, one after another."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1423
msgid ""
"Adjusts the rotation for each additional copy by the specified step value. "
"Positive values progressively rotate copies clockwise, while negative values "
"rotate them counterclockwise. When using random values, each copy will "
"receive a randomly chosen value from the defined range. When using cycle "
"values, copies will take the defined values in order, one after another."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1427
msgid ""
"Adjusts the width of each additional copy by the specified step value. "
"Positive values progressively increase the width, while negative values "
"decrease it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1431
msgid ""
"Adjusts the height of each additional copy by the specified step value. "
"Positive values progressively increase the height, while negative values "
"decrease it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1435
msgid ""
"Adjusts the parallax level of the Parallax Transition for each additional "
"copy by the specified step value. Positive values progressively increase the "
"parallax effect, while negative values decrease it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1439
msgid ""
"Adjusts the movement duration of the Parallax Transition for each additional "
"copy by the specified step value. Positive values progressively increase the "
"duration, while negative values shorten it."
msgstr ""

